151.     /// The returned frames are not guaranteed to be physically contiguous.
152.     /// User allocations are gated by the kernel watermark: if fulfilling the request would
153.     /// leave fewer than `KERNEL_WATERMARK` free frames, the allocation is rejected.
154.     ///
155.     /// # Parameters
156.     ///
157.     /// - `count`: Number of frames to allocate.
158.     /// - `frames`: Mutable reference to a pre-allocated vector into which to store those
159.     ///   frames' addresses. It should have sufficient capacity for `count` entries.
160.     ///
161.     /// # Return Values
162.     ///
163.     /// Upon success, `Ok(())` is returned and `frames` is filled with `count` frames. Upon failure, an
164.     /// error is returned and any frames allocated by this call are dropped by truncating `frames`
165.     /// back to empty.
